From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LinuxAddict <super2niia39@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ignore stale entity callbacks after a live split

A shard entity-lookup callback queued before a split can replay after the
entity was removed and re-added by the destination region. The cached old
section is then stale or never initialised, and the current region does not
own it, which halted the server with "Cannot move entity off-main" on chunk
-2147483648. Return without moving; the destination region already owns the
entity.

diff --git a/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/level/entity/EntityLookup.java b/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/level/entity/EntityLookup.java
index 7e6ab72..fed9bb5 100644
--- a/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/level/entity/EntityLookup.java
+++ b/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/level/entity/EntityLookup.java
@@ -604,6 +604,19 @@ public abstract class EntityLookup implements LevelEntityGetter<Entity> {
             return null;
         }
 
+        // Canvas start - stale entity callback after a live split
+        // A callback queued before a split can replay after the entity was
+        // removed and re-added by the destination region. The cached old
+        // section is then stale (or never initialised), and this thread does
+        // not own it. The destination region owns the entity now, so there is
+        // nothing to move here; returning also avoids the
+        // "Cannot move entity off-main" halt on chunk -2147483648.
+        if (sectionX == Integer.MIN_VALUE || sectionZ == Integer.MIN_VALUE
+            || !ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.common.util.TickThread.isTickThreadFor(this.world, sectionX, sectionZ)) {
+            return null;
+        }
+        // Canvas end - stale entity callback after a live split
+
         // ensure the old section is owned by this tick thread
         this.checkThread(sectionX, sectionZ, "Cannot move entity off-main");
 
